# Page / Full-Page Loaders

Use animated spinners for **larger loading surfaces** (route fallbacks, suspense boundaries, standalone waits).

## Components

| Component | Path | Use |
|-----------|------|-----|
| `PageSpinner` | `@/components/loaders/page-spinner` | Centered animated spinner (`react-loader-spinner` Oval) |
| `FullPageLoader` | `@/components/loaders/full-page-loader` | Full viewport wrapper around `PageSpinner` |
| `PanelRouteLoading` | `@/components/loaders/panel-route-loading` | Panel content area (not full viewport) |

## When

- `FullPageLoader` / `PageSpinner`: root `loading.tsx`, auth `loading.tsx`, custom suspense fallbacks.
- `PanelRouteLoading`: admin `loading.tsx` only.

## Pattern

```tsx
import { PageSpinner } from "@/components/loaders/page-spinner";

<Suspense fallback={<PageSpinner label="Loading data…" />}>
  <AsyncSection />
</Suspense>
```

## Do not

- Import `react-loader-spinner` directly in feature code — go through `PageSpinner`.
- Use `FullPageLoader` inside panel content (use `PanelRouteLoading`).
